From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Wed, 02 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman: pcd: dual-lane 46-byte CC-tree key packer (T-M6-8 VLAN-v6, V6-1)

First increment of extending Option A's VLAN offload (CC-tree +
HMTD, shipped 2026-08-26, plans/ASK2-VLAN-REARCH.md) from IPv4-only
to IPv4+IPv6. Staged, silicon-gated sequence (V6-1..V6-6); this is
V6-1, dormant/software-only, no behavior change.

PROBLEM: the CC-tree hardware match-table row (cc_pack_key(),
CC_KEY_SIZE=16 bytes) is IPv4-only -- PORT_ID+sip(4)+dip(4)+proto+
ports, no room for a 16-byte v6 address let alone a src/dst pair.
Both software structs that feed it -- struct fman_cc_key (ask.ko)
and struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key (this layer) -- already carry unused
is_ipv6/src_ip6[16]/dst_ip6[16] fields, and dpaa_cc_key_to_hw()
(dpaa_fman_caps.c) already correctly translates them into the
FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_IPV6 present bit. cc_pack_key() is the one link in
that chain that never got built.

FIX (this patch): a new cc_pack_key_dual() packer, entirely
additive -- cc_pack_key()/CC_KEY_SIZE are byte-for-byte untouched,
so every existing (v4-only, shipped) CC-tree consumer, including the
production VLAN feature, is unaffected. The new 46-byte layout
mirrors ask.ko's ask_fe_build_key_dual() (ask_flow_offload.c)
exactly -- the same family-discriminated dual-lane key already
silicon-proven for the routed ehash path (F-224/F-225/F-226, zero
throughput regression at this width) -- rather than inventing a new
format:

  byte 0       FAMILY: 0x80 (v4) / 0x40 (v6). Replaces cc_pack_key()'s
               byte-0 PORT_ID: port identity is already implicit in
               which per-port CC tree got installed
               (fman_cc_tree_install(fm, port_id, ...)), so PORT_ID
               was redundant key content -- safe to repurpose.
  bytes 1..4   IPv4 src, v4 keys only; zero for v6.
  bytes 5..8   IPv4 dst, v4 keys only; zero for v6.
  bytes 9..24  IPv6 src, v6 keys only; zero for v4.
  bytes 25..40 IPv6 dst, v6 keys only; zero for v4.
  byte 41      L4 proto.
  bytes 42..43 L4 src port.
  bytes 44..45 L4 dst port.

Marked __maybe_unused (matches this file's own established idiom
for "written, not yet wired in", e.g. fman_pcd.c's
__fman_pcd_fe_build_vm_chain) -- nothing calls it yet. Actually
using it requires a CC-tree KeyGen scheme reconfigured for the same
GEC-style generic extraction the ehash dual-lane scheme already
uses, which is V6-2 (silicon de-risk on cc_test, sacrificial port,
not yet done) -- the one genuinely new-territory step in this whole
increment sequence.

KUnit coverage (drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/tests/
fman_pcd_cc_dual_key_test.c, included as a trailer under
CONFIG_FSL_FMAN_PCD_KUNIT_TEST like this file's existing
fman_pcd_fe_test.c): pins the exact v4 and v6 byte layouts (computed
by hand and cross-checked against ask_fe_build_key_dual()'s
identical field offsets so the two independently-compiled layers
can't silently drift), the row stride (idx=1 doesn't overlap idx=0),
and that CC_KEY_SIZE itself is untouched at 16.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate | Risk-Tier: A (new dormant function +
KUnit-only test file; cc_pack_key()/CC_KEY_SIZE and every existing
caller of fman_cc_tree_install() untouched, byte-identical)
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c | 103 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../freescale/fman/tests/fman_pcd_cc_dual_key_test.c | 151 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 254 insertions(+)


patch-series-cleanup (2026-09-11): split. New file(s) below moved to
kernel/common/files/ as plain tracked source (a 'new file mode' hunk IS
the file's content, so tracking it directly carries no diff-drift risk
vs upstream); copied into place by ci-setup-kernel.sh before this
(now much smaller) patch applies. New files that moved:
  drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/tests/fman_pcd_cc_dual_key_test.c
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c
@@ -278,6 +278,104 @@
 }
 
 /*
+ * T-M6-8 VLAN-v6: dual-lane 46-byte CC key packer, dormant (no caller yet).
+ *
+ * cc_pack_key() above is IPv4-only and CC_KEY_SIZE=16 has no room for a
+ * 16-byte v6 address, let alone a src/dst pair. Rather than invent a new
+ * layout, this mirrors ask.ko's ask_fe_build_key_dual() (ask_flow_offload.c)
+ * byte-for-byte -- the SAME family-discriminated dual-lane key already
+ * silicon-proven for the routed ehash path (F-224/F-225/F-226, zero
+ * throughput regression at 46 bytes):
+ *
+ *   byte  0      FAMILY: 0x80 (v4) / 0x40 (v6) -- see ASK_FE_FAMILY_V4/_V6.
+ *                Replaces cc_pack_key()'s byte-0 PORT_ID: port identity is
+ *                already implicit in which per-port CC tree got installed
+ *                (fman_cc_tree_install(fm, port_id, ...)), so PORT_ID was
+ *                redundant key content to begin with -- safe to repurpose.
+ *   bytes 1..4   IPv4 src (network order), v4 keys only; zero for v6.
+ *   bytes 5..8   IPv4 dst (network order), v4 keys only; zero for v6.
+ *   bytes 9..24  IPv6 src (16B), v6 keys only; zero for v4.
+ *   bytes 25..40 IPv6 dst (16B), v6 keys only; zero for v4.
+ *   byte  41     L4 proto.
+ *   bytes 42..43 L4 src port (network order).
+ *   bytes 44..45 L4 dst port (network order).
+ *
+ * Per-key family comes from dpaa_cc_key_to_hw()'s existing
+ * FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_IPV6 present bit (already correctly set from
+ * struct fman_cc_key.is_ipv6 -- that translation was already complete;
+ * only this packer and its EKFC/GEC producer were missing).
+ *
+ * Requires a CC-tree KeyGen scheme reconfigured for the same GEC-style
+ * generic extraction the ehash dual-lane scheme already uses (T-M6-8 V6-2,
+ * silicon de-risk on cc_test, not yet done) -- this function alone changes
+ * no behavior: nothing calls it, and cc_pack_key()/CC_KEY_SIZE above are
+ * untouched, so every existing (v4-only, shipped) CC-tree consumer is
+ * byte-identical.
+ */
+#define CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL	48U
+#define CC_KEY_DUAL_FAMILY_V4	0x40U
+#define CC_KEY_DUAL_FAMILY_V6	0x60U
+
+static __maybe_unused void cc_pack_key_dual(void __iomem *match, u16 idx,
+					    const struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key *k)
+{
+	u8 key[CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL];
+	u8 msk[CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL];
+	u8 *row;
+	bool is_v6 = !!(k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_IPV6);
+
+	memset(key, 0, sizeof(key));
+	memset(msk, 0, sizeof(msk));
+
+	key[0] = is_v6 ? CC_KEY_DUAL_FAMILY_V6 : CC_KEY_DUAL_FAMILY_V4;
+	msk[0] = 0xff;
+
+	if (is_v6) {
+		/* Enforce zero in IPv4 lane [1..8] */
+		memset(&msk[1], 0xff, 8);
+
+		if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_IP) {
+			memcpy(&key[9], k->src_ip6, 16);
+			memset(&msk[9], 0xff, 16);
+		}
+		if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_IP) {
+			memcpy(&key[25], k->dst_ip6, 16);
+			memset(&msk[25], 0xff, 16);
+		}
+	} else {
+		if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_IP) {
+			memcpy(&key[1], &k->src_ip_be, 4);
+			msk[1] = msk[2] = msk[3] = msk[4] = 0xff;
+		}
+		if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_IP) {
+			memcpy(&key[5], &k->dst_ip_be, 4);
+			msk[5] = msk[6] = msk[7] = msk[8] = 0xff;
+		}
+		/* Enforce zero in IPv6 lane [9..40] */
+		memset(&msk[9], 0xff, 32);
+	}
+
+	if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_PROTO) {
+		key[41] = k->proto;
+		msk[41] = 0xff;
+	}
+	if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_PORT) {
+		key[42] = (u8)(k->src_port_be & 0xff);
+		key[43] = (u8)(k->src_port_be >> 8);
+		msk[42] = msk[43] = 0xff;
+	}
+	if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_PORT) {
+		key[44] = (u8)(k->dst_port_be & 0xff);
+		key[45] = (u8)(k->dst_port_be >> 8);
+		msk[44] = msk[45] = 0xff;
+	}
+
+	row = (u8 __force *)match + (size_t)idx * 2 * CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL;
+	memcpy_toio((void __iomem *)row, key, CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL);
+	memcpy_toio((void __iomem *)(row + CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL), msk, CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL);
+}
+
+/*
  * Encode one leaf (result) action descriptor at AD row @idx - SDK-convergent
  * RESULT AD (0115; SDK FillAdOfTypeResult, sdk_fm_cc.c:2227-2343).
  *
@@ -665,3 +763,7 @@
 	return err;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_pcd_cc_static_get_base);
+
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_FSL_FMAN_PCD_KUNIT_TEST)
+#include "tests/fman_pcd_cc_dual_key_test.c"
+#endif /* CONFIG_FSL_FMAN_PCD_KUNIT_TEST */
